    Port snakemake workflow to the vivarium monorepo packaging
    
    The albrja framework PRs (#5-#8) migrated the sim code to the monorepo
    packaging (vivarium.cluster_tools, vivarium-engine, etc.), which stranded
    the snakemake workflow: its venvs were built from pip_lock.txt files that
    pin the pre-monorepo stack. Minimal changes to make `snakemake` run end
    to end again:
    
    Environment layer:
    - Snakefile: build the two envs with `make build-env` (same machinery as
      environment.sh) into repo-local conda envs at .snakemake_envs/
      {artifact,simulation}; retire the pip_lock venv rules and
      update_packages mode. Env builds are serialized (concurrent conda
      creates corrupt the shared package cache) and env_setup exports
      JUPYTER_PATH so papermill's `-k python3` resolves to the env kernel
      instead of a user-level kernelspec in ~/.local/share/jupyter.
    - Makefile: install redis-server from conda-forge instead of `redis -c
      anaconda`; the anaconda-channel solve conflicts with a strict-priority
      conda-forge .condarc and spins for the better part of an hour.
    
    New-psimulate behavior:
    - New lsff_utils.flatten_results replaces `mv */results/*.parquet`:
      psimulate now writes per-metric directories of per-task parquet files.
    - Tolerate `psimulate restart` raising WorkflowAlreadyComplete when the
      run left nothing to retry.
    - Child sim rule output renamed person_time -> person_time_population
      (PersonTimeObserver became a PublicHealthObserver).
    - child data/loader.py honors LSFF_LBWSG_PAF_RESULTS_ROOT so the
      snakemake workflow can keep LBWSG PAF results repo-local instead of
      reading the shared-drive model root; the child_artifacts rule sets it.
    
    Data-access API and vintage changes (GBD 2021 -> GBD 2023 stack):
    - HCES raw data was catalogued out of 'Incoming Data' with renamed files.
    - covariate stillbirth_to_live_birth_ratio was retired; use
      stillbirth_28_weeks_to_live_birth_ratio (matches the sim loaders).
    - get_modelable_entity_draws requires data_type; year_id 2021 has no
      draws under release 16, use 2023; DRAWS reduced 500 -> 250.
    - Loosen vivarium_inputs' MAX_POP raw validator around the Global
      population pull (Global aggregate rows exceed the per-row bound).
    - dalys_by_scenario: the child model must contribute no YLDs, but the
      current results system writes explicit zero rows where older versions
      wrote an empty table; assert on values instead of emptiness.
    
    Correctness fix:
    - lsff_utils/hemoglobin_distribution.py compensated for the reversed
      MirroredGumbel CDF (ihmeuw/risk_distributions#62) with `1 - cdf(x)`.
      The monorepo vivarium-risk-distributions fixed the bug upstream, so
      the workaround was re-inverting a correct CDF (uniform ~0.59 error,
      caught by the notebook's own PDF/CDF consistency check).
    
    NOTE: the notebooks now pull GBD 2023 where they pulled GBD 2021, so
    regenerated results shift with the data vintage.
    
